.TH "GOREECLOUD-TERMINAL" 1 "21 August 2026"
.SH NAME
goreecloud-terminal \- launch GoreeCloud Terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B goreecloud-terminal
.RI [OPTION]...
[\-\- PROGRAM ARGUMENTS]
.br
.B goreecloud-terminal ssh
.I TARGET
.RI [SSH_ARGUMENT ...]
.br
.B goreecloud-terminal ssh-tab
.I TARGET
.RI [SSH_ARGUMENT ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B goreecloud-terminal
is the canonical command-line launcher for GoreeCloud Terminal.
.PP
For ordinary arguments, it forwards the command line unchanged to the inherited
.B ptyxis
runtime so GoreeCloud can provide a first-party command name without prematurely breaking compatibility-sensitive runtime, helper, packaging, D-Bus, or rollback behavior.
.PP
GoreeCloud Terminal is a GoreeCloud-maintained open-source fork of Ptyxis. The upstream runtime foundation and GPL attribution remain preserved.
.SH SSH WORKFLOWS
The
.B ssh
subcommand opens a new GoreeCloud Terminal window running the system
.BR ssh (1)
client.
.PP
The
.B ssh-tab
subcommand opens the OpenSSH session as a new tab in the existing GoreeCloud Terminal instance.
.PP
TARGET may be a hostname, address, user@hostname value, or a Host alias configured through standard OpenSSH configuration such as ~/.ssh/config. Remaining arguments are passed to the system ssh command without GoreeCloud reinterpretation.
.PP
OpenSSH remains responsible for host configuration, host-key verification, authentication, keys, agents, ports, proxy settings, forwarding, and connection policy. GoreeCloud Terminal does not store SSH passwords or private keys and does not replace OpenSSH configuration.
.SH COMPATIBILITY
The inherited
.B ptyxis
command remains installed during the current development and migration stage. Existing scripts and workflows may continue using it.
.PP
New GoreeCloud documentation and normal user workflows should prefer
.B goreecloud-terminal
unless a compatibility test specifically requires the inherited command.
.SH OPTIONS
Except for the GoreeCloud
.B ssh
and
.B ssh-tab
subcommands, command-line options and program arguments are passed directly to the
.B ptyxis
runtime. For the inherited option set, see:
.PP
.BR ptyxis (1)
.SH EXAMPLES
Open GoreeCloud Terminal:
.PP
.nf
goreecloud-terminal
.fi
.PP
Open a new window:
.PP
.nf
goreecloud-terminal --new-window
.fi
.PP
Run a command in a terminal:
.PP
.nf
goreecloud-terminal -- bash -lc 'printf "hello from GoreeCloud Terminal\\n"'
.fi
.PP
Open a standard OpenSSH session in a new window using an OpenSSH Host alias:
.PP
.nf
goreecloud-terminal ssh server-alias
.fi
.PP
Open the same style of session in a new tab:
.PP
.nf
goreecloud-terminal ssh-tab server-alias
.fi
.PP
Pass an additional OpenSSH option:
.PP
.nf
goreecloud-terminal ssh server-alias -p 2222
.fi
.SH SECURITY
Do not place reusable passwords, private-key material, tokens, or other secrets directly in command-line arguments. Standard OpenSSH and operating-system credential controls remain authoritative.
.SH PROJECT
GoreeCloud repository:
.br
https://github.com/GoreeCloud/goreecloud-terminal
.PP
Canonical upstream Ptyxis source:
.br
https://gitlab.gnome.org/chergert/ptyxis
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ptyxis (1),
.BR ssh (1),
.BR ssh_config (5)
